Z||000011||AusFiero||06-09-2001||04:32 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>Simmons wheels , from australia<P>Also try HRE<BR>and Fikse.. a little more than the the simmons , but equally as nice if not better.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Simmons Kick Ass. Choice of all race cars in this country. Well except the rice boys who must have Euro wheels or Jap wheels.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>If you are really interested in them Ferg I could probably try to dig you up a simmons brochure from a local tyre joint. Is a lot more available than what is on their website.<P>E-Mail me if you want one.<P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
Z||000012||kslish||06-09-2001||05:31 AM||||Miriamme is a real proud of her Fiero.  I talked to her some at the Columbus, OH FOCOA show in 1999.  It won best of show that year I believe.  She was also at Carlisle last year (but not this year and I heard that the engine is blown too...the 21lbs of boost she was running probably has something to do with that).<P>I have a photo of her display stand, here is the info off of it....<P>-----------------<P>Car name: DVLISH<P>Year: 1986 Pontiac Fiero GT<P>Wheels: Simmons OM17 rims, Front 17x7.5 and rear 17x9.0, Bridgestone Potenza S02 215/45ZR17 (front) and 275/40ZR17 (rear)<P>Brakes: Custom 12" vented disc brakes<P>Engine: 1993 modified GM aluminum head 3.1L V6 turbo, 375bhp at 21psi, connected to a Muncie 5-speed<P>Engine Mods: Garrett T3 Turbo, block bored .020 over, 7.0:1 low compression forged pistons, balenced and blueprinted, heads ported and polished, Crane Compucam 2000, Lucas 31LB injectors, Paxton adjustable fuel regulator, Electromotive Tech II Ignition system, Jet-Hot coated exhaust manifolds, custom stainless steel exhaust<P>Chassis: Custom tubular control arms with urethane bushings, full adjustable coil over shocks & struts, Suspension Technique sway bars<P>Interior: Cyberdyne digital guages, Recaro seats, Momo accessories & graphite accents<P>----------------<P>Here are some links to more pics I have of the car (note, you may have to cut and paste these addresses directly into your browser because NBCi doesn't like direct linking of images).<P>Exterior:<BR> <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carlisle25b.jpg">  <BR> <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FOCOA53.jpg">  <BR> <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FOCOA52.jpg">  <P>Front suspension:<BR> <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FOCOA51.jpg">  <P>Note: I do believe that the control arm and coil-over suspension components are slightly modified RCC units.<P>Rear suspension:<BR> <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FOCOA50.jpg">  <P>Engine:<BR> <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FOCOA48.jpg">  <P><BR>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR> <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A> <P><p>[This message has been edited by kslish (edited 06-09-2001).]||||reg||1
